Z||000000||87gt guy||12-27-2001||02:20 PM||||Hey guys, I am fixing up my 87 gt that was sitting for over a year. It runs beutiful, but I can't exactly figure out what this sensor is. Only one wire is connected out of 3. Also, my "service engine soon" light comes on after about 15 mins of driving. How can I trouble shoot that?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://stpstp1.tripod.com/fiero.jpg"> <BR>AOL SN: STPSTP1||||reg||5
Z||000001||87gt guy||12-27-2001||02:22 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://downloads.members.tripod.com/stpstp1/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||12-27-2001||02:31 PM||||I can't really tell from the pic (it's a little dark on my comouter), but it looks like it is the oil pressure sending unit.  Does your oil pressure gauge work?  <P>As far as teh engine code goes.....you'll have to check teh codes at the ALDL (under panel with cigarette lighter).  Since you say it comes on after driving it for 15 minutes I suspect a code 32, which is the EGR system.  This code is almost always caused by a vacuum leak, so check all vacuum lines, etc. for cracks or missing lines.  The rubber line that attaches the EGR solenoid to the firewall is usually the culprit.<P>Good luck! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87gt guy||12-27-2001||02:35 PM||||thanks, thats what I thuoght because my oil pressure gauge never moves. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||12-27-2001||02:36 PM||||Damn... I'm just a little too slow today... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sensor.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe Torma||12-27-2001||02:56 PM||||Yup, oil pressure sensor.||||reg||1
